    image: "/poi-images/akim-oda-cities-v2.webp",
    description: { de: "Akim Oda ist die Hauptstadt des Birim Central Municipal District, bekannt für ihren großen Baum.", hu: "Akim Oda a Birim Középső önkormányzati kerület fővárosa, nagy fájáról ismert.", ro: "Akim Oda este capitala districtului municipal Birim Central, cunoscut pentru marele său copac.", en: "Akim Oda is the capital of the Birim Central Municipal District, known for its big tree." },
    facts: {
      de: ["Die Stadt Akim Oda hat eine geschätzte Bevölkerung von über 51231.", "Es ist ein bedeutendes städtisches Zentrum in der Region GH-EP Ghanas."],
      hu: ["Akim Oda városának becsült lakossága több mint 51231 fő.", "Jelentős városközpont Ghána GH-EP régiójában."],
      ro: ["Orașul Akim Oda are o populație estimată la peste 51231.", "Este un centru urban semnificativ în regiunea GH-EP din Ghana.", "en: The city of Akim Oda has an estimated population of over 51231.", "It is a significant urban center in the GH-EP region of Ghana."],
      en: ["Capital of the Birim Central Municipal District", "Estimated population exceeds 51,231", "Region is known for the world's largest Badi (Big Tree)", "Major center for timber and cocoa production"]
    }, image: "/poi-images/akim-oda-cities-v2.webp",
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Akim Oda ist das pulsierende Zentrum der Birim Central Municipal in der Eastern Region und historisch bekannt für den Handel mit Tropenholz und Diamanten. Der Markt in Oda ist einer der größten der Region, besonders beliebt für den Handel mit Kassava und Palmöl, die im feuchten, dichten Waldklima gedeihen. Die Stadt war jahrzehntelang Standort der größten Sägemühle Westafrikas, doch der Rückgang der Wälder hat zu einem wirtschaftlichen Umdenken in Richtung nachhaltigerer Landwirtschaft geführt. Umwelt K7 — Waldwirtschaft.",
      hu: "Akim Oda (vagy Akyem Oda) egy fontos agrár- és erdészeti központ a Keleti Régió sűrű trópusi esőerdei övezetében. A település az ősi Akyem Kotoku állam székhelye, amely a Birim folyó mentén terül el. A város gazdaságát évtizedeken át a fakitermelés, a kakaó és a gyémántbányászat mozgatta. Gazdaság K7 — erdei nyersanyagok.",
      ro: "Akim Oda, sau simplu Oda, reprezintă inima vibrantă a subgrupului etnic Akyem din Regiunea de Est. Situat în mijlocul unei zone împădurite bogate, orașul și-a construit prosperitatea datorită industriei forestiere intensive, procesării lemnului și agriculturii comerciale masive bazate pe cacao. Dincolo de industrie, Oda uimește printr-un record mondial puțin cunoscut: aici se află cel mai mare arbore de Badi (Big Tree) din lume, o minune naturală veche de sute de ani. Economie K6 — exploatarea resurselor regenerabile.",
      en: "Akim Oda is a bustling commercial and historical town located in the Eastern Region, functioning as the capital of the Birim Central Municipal District. It serves as the traditional capital of the Akyem Kotoku state. The town is situated in a dense tropical rainforest zone and has historically been a major center for Ghana's timber extraction and sawmilling industry, alongside extensive cocoa production. The nearby forest famously contains the 'Big Tree', believed to be one of the largest and oldest trees in West Africa. Akim Oda's vibrant central market and transport terminals make it the economic nerve center of the Birim River basin. Geography K7 — forestry and cash crop economies."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Zentrum der Birim Central Municipal", "Historisch bekannt für Tropenholz und Diamanten", "Einer der größten Märkte der Region", "Handel mit Kassava und Palmöl", "Einst größte Sägemühle Westafrikas", "Wirtschaftlicher Wandel durch Waldrückgang"],
      hu: ["Az Akyem Kotoku hagyományos terület központja", "A Birim folyó völgyében, esőerdei környezetben fekszik", "Híres nagy kiterjedésű faipari feldolgozóiról", "Ghána legvastagabb törzsű fája (Akim Oda Big Tree) a közelben áll", "Lakossága mintegy 60 ezer fő", "Történelmileg a ghánai gyémántkereskedelem egyik gócpontja volt"],
      ro: ["Aproape de oraș se găsește Big Tree, cel mai voluminos copac din Africa de Vest.", "Este reședința șefului tradițional al poporului Akyem Kotoku.", "Procesarea cherestelei constituie fundația economică a orașului.", "Zona se bucură de un nivel de ploaie optim pentru pădurile tropicale.", "Există fabrici puternice specializate pe prelucrarea primară a lemnului.", "Orașul deține unul dintre cele mai longevive și vibrante târguri locale."],
      en: ["Capital of the Birim Central Municipal District in the Eastern Region.", "Serves as the traditional seat of the paramount chief of the Akyem Kotoku.", "Historically a major hub for the commercial timber and sawmilling industries.", "Located near the famous 'Big Tree' in the Esen Epam Forest Reserve.", "Situated within the highly fertile Birim River basin.", "The local economy is heavily dependent on cocoa, palm oil, and timber."]
    }
