    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Akwatia, in der Eastern Region, ist das Herz der ghanaischen Diamantenindustrie. Die Stadt wurde in den 1920er Jahren um eine riesige Diamantenmine der Consolidated African Selection Trust herum erbaut. Mehr als ein halbes Jahrhundert lang lieferte die Mine Industrie-Diamanten in alle Welt, was der Stadt einen gewissen Wohlstand brachte. Heute ist die Mine weitgehend erschöpft, und die Bevölkerung wendet sich zunehmend dem illegalen Kleinstbergbau oder der Landwirtschaft zu. Wirtschaft K7 — Diamantenabbau.",
      hu: "Akwatia a Keleti Régió leghíresebb gyémántbányászati központja, amely a Birim folyó völgyében fekszik. A város fejlődését az 1920-as években felfedezett hatalmas ipari gyémántlelőhelyek indították el. Noha a nagyüzemi bányászat mára visszaesett, a kisüzemi ásás máig a helyi gazdaság alapja. Gazdaság K8 — drágakő-kitermelés.",
      ro: "Akwatia a fost mult timp echivalent cu un cuvânt magic în Ghana: diamante. Situat ferm în Regiunea de Est, subsolul său argilos a fost răscolit decenii la rând de operațiuni masive de extragere a diamantelor. Astăzi, deși marile campanii miniere s-au estompat, moștenirea minerală este evidentă în casele vechi destinate lucrătorilor și utilajele ruginite abandonate în peisaj. Mineritul informal de diamante sprijină încă visul multor tineri ce continuă să caute pe albia râului Birim. Economie K7 — orașe mono-industriale.",
      en: "Akwatia is a highly significant mining town in the Eastern Region, serving as the capital of the Denkyembour District. It is internationally famous as the historic epicenter of Ghana's diamond mining industry. Large-scale commercial extraction of alluvial diamonds began here in the 1920s under the Consolidated African Selection Trust (CAST). While the massive corporate operations have significantly scaled down in recent decades, the town's landscape remains defined by vast mined-out areas, and a massive informal artisanal mining sector continues to operate. The legacy of diamonds has profoundly shaped the town's demography, infrastructure, and environmental challenges. Geography K7 — precious gem extraction."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      de: ["Herz der ghanaischen Diamantenindustrie", "Mine 1920er Jahre erbaut (CAST)", "Mehr als 50 Jahre Industrie-Diamanten geliefert", "Heute sind Minen weitgehend erschöpft", "Zunehmender illegaler Kleinstbergbau", "Liegt in der Eastern Region"],
      hu: ["Ghána elsőszámú történelmi gyémántkitermelő városa", "A Keleti Régió (Eastern Region) Denkyembour körzetének központja", "A kitermelt gyémántok nagyrészt ipari minőségűek voltak", "A Consolidated Diamonds bányavállalat évtizedekig uralta a várost", "A település lakossága mintegy 25 ezer fő", "A bányászat következtében a környező táj erősen átalakult"],
      ro: ["Mina de diamante de aici a dominat istoric piața din Africa de Vest.", "Orașul este poziționat strategic pe bazinul fluviului Birim.", "Decăderea companiei miniere GCD a transformat orașul în anii 1990.", "Astăzi mii de lucrători recurg la prospectarea manuală după diamante libere.", "Populația menține o viață destul de rurală, îmbinând agricultura de subzistență.", "Zona a atras lucrători migranți diversificați din statele francofone nordice."],
      en: ["Capital of the Denkyembour District in the Eastern Region of Ghana.", "Historically the premier center for diamond mining in West Africa.", "Commercial diamond extraction began in the area during the 1920s.", "The local landscape is heavily scarred by decades of intensive alluvial mining.", "Currently supports a massive informal artisanal mining (galamsey) economy.", "Located within the fertile Birim River valley, which hosts the diamond deposits."]
    }
