      en: "Denu is a vital coastal and border town in the Volta Region, serving as the capital of the Ketu South Municipal District. It is situated almost contiguously with the massive border town of Aflao, functioning practically as its administrative and residential twin. Denu's economy is highly diversified; while it heavily benefits from the intense cross-border trade logistics of Aflao, it also maintains a robust traditional artisanal fishing industry along its sandy shores. The town features significant coconut plantations and serves as a critical transport staging area for goods moving between the Ghanaian interior and Togo. Geography K7 — border logistics and coastal trade."
